GOVERNMENT OF INDIA 
MINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION 
Lok Sabha 
UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 2359 
 ( TO BE ANSWERED ON THE  13th March 2025 )  
AVAILABILITY OF IN-FLIGHT WI-FI 
2359.    SHRI TANGELLA UDAY SRINIVAS              
             SMT D K ARUNA                           
Will the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION 
be pleased to state:- 
(a) whether it is true that AIR INDIA rolled out Wi -Fi internet connectivity 
services on board domestic flights operated in its fleet such as Air bus A 
350, Boeing 787-9 and Airbus A 321neo and if so, the details thereof along 
with the present status of its implementation; 

(b) the steps being taken by the Government to extend the said facility to 
both domestic and international flights in a time -bound manner, sector -
wise; 

(c) the details of airlines in the country offering in -flight Wi -Fi services 
along with its availability across routes/specific flights; 

(d) whether the said Wi-Fi services are free/paid and the internet access is 
unrestricted/limited to certain content and if so, the details thereof; 

(e) the role of the Government in granting regulatory approvals and 
coordinating with telecom service providers and airlines for the rollout of 
in-flight Wi-Fi services; 

(f) whether the Government has any plans to mandate and incentivize 
Indian carriers to provide in -flight Wi-Fi services, especially on long -haul 
and international routes and if so, the details thereof; and 

(g) the comparison of in-flight Wi-Fi availability and accessibility on Indi an 
carriers versus global airlines along with the measures being taken to 
bring Indian airlines at par with international standards? 
ANSWER 

Minister of State in the Ministry of CIVIL AVIATION      (Shri 
Murlidhar Mohol) 
(a): Yes, Air India has rolled out Wi-Fi on domestic and international 
flights.   This service is being offered on A350, A321 and B789 type 
aircraft, which are equipped to provide Wi-Fi on board.; 
; 
(b): The Government has notified the amended Rule 29B of the Aircraft 
Rules, 1937 vide GSR N o. 142(E) dated 21.02.2020 for permitting the use 
of internet services by passengers on board an aircraft in flight through 
Wi-Fi for use of smartphone in flight mode or airplane mode.; 
; 
In compliance of Rule 29B of the Aircraft Rules, 1937, the detailed 
requirements have been issued as Civil Aviation Requirements (CAR) 
Section 5 Series X Part I dated 24.11.2020 for the use of internet service 
through Wi-Fi.; 
; 
Further, there is no distinction regarding use of inflight Wi -Fi connectivity 
for domestic and international operations. 
; 
It is for the airlines to provide the internet connectivity in compliance with 
Rule 29B of the Aircraft Rules, 1937 during the flight.; 
; 
(c): Only Air India is providing Wi -Fi services in India, on certain types of 
aircraft such as A350, A321 and B789.; 
; 
The availability of Wi -Fi on board is indicated to the passenger on the air 
ticket.  These aircraft are not deployed on specific routes and hence such 
services are not assured on any specific route or flight number.; 
; 
(d): Air India is providing free internet on board on aircraft which are 
equipped with Wi-Fi equipment for browsing only.; 
; 
(e): Operators have to comply with the Directorate General of Civil 
Aviation (DGCA) Civil Aviation Requirements (CAR) and also with the 
guidelines/ rules issued by the Telecom Department in order to operate 
such Wi -Fi service.  Permission is accorded once the operator 
demonstrates compliance with these requirements.; 
; 
(f): There is no such proposal to mandate or incentivize Indian carriers to  
provide in-flight Wi-Fi services by DGCA.; 

; 
(g): DGCA does not monitor availability and accessibility of such services 
and only provides permission to operate Wi-Fi services to Indian carriers. 
